    <!-- ==== Service Faq Section Start ==== -->
    <section class="rs-service-faq pt-120 pb-120">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="row align-items-center">
                <div class="col-lg-6 wow fadeInLeft" data-wow-duration="1.5s" data-wow-delay="0.0s">
                    <div class="section-title-2 section-title-3">
                        <span> Your Answer</span>
                        <h2 class="title">Frequently asked questions & Searching answer.</h2>
                    </div>
                    <div class="rs-faq__wrapper">
                        <div class="accordion active">
                            <div class="accordion_tab active">
                                01. What health parameters does SAFIRA Band monitor?
                                <div class="accordion_arrow">
                                    <i class="ri-add-fill"></i>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="accordion_content">
                                <div class="accordion_item">
                                    <p>SAFIRA Band continuously tracks blood pressure, heart rate, oxygen levels (SpO₂), body temperature, sleep patterns, and stress levels. These insights help users and caregivers proactively manage health conditions.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="accordion">
                            <div class="accordion_tab">
                                02. How accurate is the fall detection feature in SAFIRA Band?
                                <div class="accordion_arrow">
                                    <i class="ri-add-fill"></i>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="accordion_content">
                                <div class="accordion_item">
                                    <p>SAFIRA Band uses AI-powered 6-axis motion sensors to accurately distinguish real falls from normal daily movements. A 30-second cancellation window is provided to avoid false alerts before notifying emergency contacts.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="accordion">
                            <div class="accordion_tab">
                                03. Can Guardian Band be used without a smartphone?
                                <div class="accordion_arrow">
                                    <i class="ri-add-fill"></i>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="accordion_content">
                                <div class="accordion_item">
                                    <p>Yes, SAFIRA Band supports independent operation using built-in 4G LTE connectivity. It can send SOS alerts, share live location, and contact emergency services even when a smartphone is not nearby.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="accordion">
                            <div class="accordion_tab">
                                04. Can caregivers or family members monitor the user remotely?
                                <div class="accordion_arrow">
                                    <i class="ri-add-fill"></i>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="accordion_content">
                                <div class="accordion_item">
                                    <p>Yes, authorized caregivers and family members can monitor alerts, location, and health data through the SAFIRA Band mobile app or web dashboard. Access is fully controlled by the user to maintain privacy.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
